  "body": "Found while fixing #561 (PR #566).\n\n**Today:** turning a part on the Model page by an angle that isn't a quarter turn rotates its box or cylinder stock rigidly with it (`crates/app/src/commands/move_model.rs:105-108`). A stock square to the machine ends up tilted, and ops then cut a tilted blank's top. #566 fixed this for locate only (`stock_follow.rs`: a stock square to the setup keeps its orientation and is refitted with each side's allowance). Plain `MoveModel` keeps the rigid follow, and `commands_undo::moving_one_part_carries_existing_stock_and_undo_restores_both` pins it.\n\n**Expected:** decide whether a Model-page turn should use the same square-stock rule. Likely yes: a vise clamps the blank square. If it changes, the existing pin is updated with the decision recorded.\n\n**Done means:** a test turns a part with a square stock by 30° on the Model page and checks the stock stays square, or the rigid behaviour is kept and documented with a by-name note to the user.",
